{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793642556,"nonce":"6zsaHAcNawVVj/cW9pRjU3yFd3U=","title":"A rule keyed on a bound attribute or class does not apply display","message":"With the stylesheet .x[data-hidden] { display: none; }, a div.x with .attr(\"data-hidden\", \"\") lays out as display none (zero bounds, is_display_none true), but the same div with .attr_when(\"data-hidden\", \"\", signal(true)) keeps its 50x20 box: the dynamic class layer applies the rule's visual properties but not display. Found when cn chart legends meant to hide by [data-hidden] stayed visible; the chart now builds its legend with .show(..) instead.\n\nReproducer: RenderTree from the two divs above, set_stylesheet, apply_stylesheet_layout_overrides, apply_stylesheet_base_styles, drain take_pending_partial_prop_updates into apply_partial_property_updates, compute_layout, then compare layout_tree.is_display_none(node). Likely other layout properties a dynamic rule sets (width, height, padding, flex) need the same check.","files":null}]}